{
  "id": "COMPOUND:27962 - PROTEIN:5829",
  "verbalization": "n-Octyl sulfate is implicated in the relationship with CHP-134 through a series of molecular interactions involving sialyltransferase enzymes. The evidence suggests that n-Octyl sulfate acts as a target for CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide. These compounds are themselves targets of CHP-134, indicating a complex cascade of interactions where n-Octyl sulfate indirectly influences CHP-134 through the enzymatic pathways it engages with. The evidence supports a mechanism where n-Octyl sulfate may modulate the activity of these enzymes, potentially affecting the downstream signaling or metabolic processes that CHP-134 targets. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of sialyltransferase enzymes in mediating the interaction between n-Octyl sulfate and CHP-134, suggesting a possible role in cellular signaling or metabolic regulation.",
